        "type": "the-purpose",
        "title": "Untitled",
        "body": "This topic set explores the Space Shuttle Program not through the lens of complex physics or engineering mathematics, but as a monumental human endeavor. The topics focus on the political, strategic, and organizational decisions that defined its creation, its operational triumphs, and its tragic failures. We will investigate its role as a construction vehicle, a scientific laboratory, and a symbol of national prestige. The goal is to understand the *why* and *so what* of the Shuttle—its profound impact on international collaboration, its cultural legacy, and how its retirement directly paved the way for the modern commercial spaceflight era.",
